  "notes": "Hisense E5Q Pro (internal model \"VIDAA_TV\", MediaTek MT9653), VIDAA on Android 11, firmware 02.02.70.01\nSecurity patch 2022-09-05. China-market set: a VIDAA/Android hybrid with no Google TV launcher,\nso the stock home is com.jamdeo.tv.vod and the tuner app is com.jamdeo.tv.livetv; both are left\nalone here. The VIDAA UI keeps working; this list only removes the ad, telemetry, push and\npreloaded-content layer on top of it.\nSame VIDAA_TV / MT9653 / 02.02.70.01 build as examples/vidda-mt9653/, which goes further (it also\nswaps the launcher); this list is the conservative subset that keeps the stock home.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/hisense-e5q-pro/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/hisense-e5q-pro/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nApplied and lived with for a few days: no crashes, normal boot, and the inputs / HDMI-CEC and the\nSogou TV keyboard kept working. OTA (com.jamdeo.updateservice, com.hisense.usbupgrade,\ncom.hisense.playerupdate) is left enabled on purpose so firmware updates still arrive.\n\nAlso useful on this firmware, as an extra ad-block flag (not a package):\nsettings put global com.hisense.service.ad_block 1\nHisense advertising",
